Key Takeaway for Architects

Systems break when security is treated as a checklist rather than a holistic, end-to-end pipeline. To immunize an application against these hyper-hidden vectors, developers must establish a single, server-controlled source of truth:
1. Cryptographically sign and verify all webhook/callback metadata directly from the provider.
2. Implement strict database transactional isolation levels (SERIALIZABLE or pessimistic explicit locking) to combat concurrency anomalies.
3. Enforce strict server-side data validation and typecasting across every internal microservice boundary, completely ignoring parameters passing through the client device.
